=== PARITY (vs web ChargeStatusLiveWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (ChargeStatusSource -> ChargeStatusModel):
    useVehicles, useVehicleState (refetch 5s), useChargingSessionsPaginated(limit 1), useUnits,
    useTranslation. The production app wires ChargeStatusSource over the KMP vehicle-state live query +
    charging-session store + unit preferences; the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> ChargeMetrics.project mirrors the web `metrics` memo exactly: power = charger_power (kW),
    voltage = null, amps = null (web hardcodes both -> em-dash cells), energyAdded = total_energy_added_wh
    ?? 0 (SI Wh), timeToFull = time_to_full_charge ?? 0 (h), rate = charge_rate ?? 0 (SI m), battery =
    battery_level ?? 0. ChargeConvert reproduces convertDistanceFromSI (METERS_PER_KM 1000 / METERS_PER_MILE
    1609.344) and convertEnergyFromSI (Wh/1000) to the digit. ChargeFormat.timeRemaining is a 1:1 port of the
    web `formatTime` ('—' / Nm / Nh / Nh Mm). SI stays on the wire; conversion happens at the display boundary
    (useUnits -> ChargeUnits.distance), per the unit-conversion contract. Verified by executed XCTest.
  Composition -> shell chrome (bolt icon + "Charge Status" title [hidden when compact] + freshness chip +
    refresh + optional Open) · 1x1 CompactChargingView (pulsing charge glyph + kW + battery%) · 1x1
    CompactIdleView (plug + battery% + "Not Charging") · full FullChargingView (status header: charge glyph +
    "Charging" success chip + battery%; primary kW; 2x2 metric grid Voltage/Current/Time Left/Added; + a tall
    row Rate/Battery when rows>=2) · full IdleView (plug + "Not Charging" + battery% + "Last Session" recap when
    a prior session is cached). isCompact/isTall are computed from the requested size, like the web prop.
  Shared components -> reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSTone / TSSkeleton +
    ContentUnavailableView (compiled against the REAL apps/apple tokens + TSTone badges in the typechecks
    below). ChargeChip mirrors the TSBadge tokens, extended to take a pre-localized String (our per-surface
    table) + a leading SF Symbol the LocalizedStringKey-only TSBadge can't express.
    Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (no chart/map on this surface).
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton chrome) · empty ("No charge data") · error (retry affordance) ·
    stale (chip + banner) · offline (cached value + chip + banner) · content (charging|idle × compact|full).
    Model phase resolution keeps cached content visible behind refresh/errors, matching the web shell
    (state present -> content for every load status; state absent -> loading/empty/error).
  i18n -> all source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    widget.chargeStatusLive, noChargeData, notCharging, charging, voltage, amps, timeRemaining, energyAdded,
    chargeRate, batteryLevel, lastSession -> ALL PRESENT in ChargeStatusLiveWidget.strings (+ registry
    description + native chrome: open/chargeLive/chargeStale/chargeOffline/chargeRefresh/chargeRetry/
    chargeLoading/noChargeDataHint/chargeErrorTitle/chargeOfflineBanner/chargeStaleBanner/chargeOpenA11y).
    No English literals in native code (verbatim from the facade). Key cross-check: used == declared.
  a11y -> the content carries a combined charging/idle summary (ChargeAccessibility.summary); each metric
    cell a combined "label: value"; the freshness chip + every button (refresh / retry / open) an
    accessibilityLabel; Dynamic Type via tokens; the charge glyph uses .symbolEffect(.pulse) which respects
